." cal(1)
.TH CAL 1 "2026-04-23" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cal \- display calendars
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cal
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [[ month ] year ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cal
prints a calendar for the current month by default.
With one numeric operand it prints an entire year.
With two numeric operands it prints the specified month of the specified year.
.PP
Substrate
.B cal
supports mixed Julian/Gregorian rendering with a configurable reform date.
In the default mixed mode, dates before the reform are interpreted in the Julian calendar and dates on or after the reform are interpreted in the Gregorian calendar. Dates in the skipped transition gap are omitted from output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -1
Display a single month.
This is the default when no explicit year-only mode is selected.
.TP
.B -3
Display the previous, current, and next month side by side.
.TP
.B -y
Display an entire year in a three-column layout.
.TP
.B -m
Start weeks on Monday.
.TP
.B -s
Start weeks on Sunday.
This is the default.
.TP
.B -j
Display day-of-year ordinals instead of day-of-month numbers.
.TP
.B -w
Display ISO week numbers in the left column.
.TP
.BI -n " NUM"
Display
.I NUM
months starting at the base month.
.TP
.BI -A " NUM"
Display
.I NUM
months after the base month.
.TP
.BI -B " NUM"
Display
.I NUM
months before the base month.
.TP
.BR -h , " --no-highlight"
Disable highlighting of today's date.
.TP
.BI --color = WHEN
Control ANSI highlighting behavior.
.I WHEN
may be
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
.TP
.B --gregorian
Use Gregorian calendar rules exclusively.
.TP
.B --julian
Use Julian calendar rules exclusively.
.TP
.BR -p , " --reform=" DATE
Set the first Gregorian calendar date used in mixed mode.
.I DATE
must use the form
.BR YYYY-MM-DD .
.TP
.B --help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display version information and exit.
.SH REFORM HANDLING
The default reform date is
.BR 1752-09-14 .
Under that default, September 1752 omits the dates 3 through 13 inclusive.
.PP
For a mixed-mode month, a textual date is shown only if it exists either as a Julian date before the reform or as a Gregorian date on or after the reform.
.SH HIGHLIGHTING
When highlighting is enabled,
.B cal
renders today's date with reverse-video ANSI escape sequences.
In
.B auto
color mode this happens only when standard output is a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
cal
Display the current month.
.TP
cal 2024
Display the entire 2024 calendar.
.TP
cal 9 1752
Display September 1752 using the default British/American reform gap.
.TP
cal -3 1 2024
Display December 2023, January 2024, and February 2024.
.TP
cal --julian 2 1900
Display February 1900 using Julian leap-year rules.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Usage error or rendering failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR date (1),
.BR strftime (3),
.BR localtime (3)